{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124413","id":4833593462,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIBrIdg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124413","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124413.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124413.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124413","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124413/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124413/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124413/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f7b0125893384d0b81a0fcbf5c5a88c252c32e72","number":124413,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Use effective sample count when resolving MSAA depth","user":{"login":"upalvstavai","id":322082323,"node_id":"U_kgDOEzKWEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/322082323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai","html_url":"https://github.com/upalvstavai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/upalvstavai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\n\nOn Apple GPUs that do not support 8x MSAA, the rendering driver creates 4-sample textures while the depth resolve shaders still use the requested sample count of 8. The resolve then reads nonexistent samples 4 through 7, corrupting the resolved depth and breaking effects such as Proximity Fade.\n\n- Closes #123478\n\n## Additional information\n\nQuery the actual sample count from the bound multisample depth texture in both compute and raster resolve shaders, capped by the requested count. This keeps the existing push-constant interface while preventing out-of-range sample fetches after a rendering backend lowers the requested MSAA level.\n\nTested on an Apple M1 (Apple7) with Metal 4.0 and Forward+. The issue's MRP was reproduced before the change with MSAA 8x, while MSAA 4x rendered correctly. After the change:\n\n- the 8x and 4x captures from the patched build were pixel-identical;\n- key fade-profile probes matched the known-good capture within one RGB level;\n- pixels with a maximum channel error above 30 in the affected ROI fell from 34,550 to 871 (97.5% reduction compared with the original 8x capture);\n- the editor log contained no shader errors, `SCRIPT ERROR`, or Metal validation errors.\n\nAI assistance was used for repository search, root-cause analysis, implementing the small shader change, and assembling the test evidence. The final diff was reviewed in Codex by an independent second pass. The patched engine was compiled locally and the visual result was verified against the issue's MRP with fixed camera state and pixel-level comparisons.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-12T18:43:04Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T20:56:28Z","closed_at":"2026-10-12T18:56:27Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commi